<h2 id="desirables-section-schemes-cohomology" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="02BE">113.6</span> Cohomology of schemes</h2>

<p>
There is already a chapter on cohomology of quasi-coherent sheaves, see Cohomology of Schemes, Section <a href="/tag/01X7" data-tag="01X7">30.1</a>. We have a chapter discussing the derived category of quasi-coherent sheaves on a scheme, see Derived Categories of Schemes, Section <a href="/tag/08CV" data-tag="08CV">36.1</a>. We have a chapter discussing duality for Noetherian schemes and relative duality for morphisms of schemes, see Duality for Schemes, Section <a href="/tag/0DWF" data-tag="0DWF">48.1</a>. We also have chapters on étale cohomology of schemes and on crystalline cohomology of schemes. But most of the material in these chapters is very basic and a lot more could/should be added there. 
</p>
